    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing: US operating SaaS/software company; no prior DCF, no memory entry - fresh build). FY0 = FY2025 actuals; the FY2026 growth year is anchored to guidance (revenue $2.535-2.575B, mid $2.555B = +9.5%, includes For The Record acquired April 2026 for $212.7M). Adjusted EBITDA margin is pre-SBC: FY2025 GAAP operating income $357.7M + D&A $138.4M + SBC $151.3M = $647.3M = 27.8% (H1-2026 27.8%). Reported FCF follows Tyler's own definition: OCF $653.5M - PP&E capex $16.0M - capitalized software $16.8M = $620.7M (26.6%). Owner FCF = 620.7 - 197.5 SBC incl. withholding - 34.9 interest income (other non-operating income $37.6M less $2.7M rental income) = $388.3M (16.6%). Interest income is stripped because the $1,015M liquid pile is added back in the bridge. ANCHORS: 2026-06-30 balance sheet - cash $895.4M + short-term investments $74.7M + long-term investments $45.2M = $1,015.3M liquid; debt = new convertible senior notes $1,437.5M face (carrying $1,408.7M; the $600M 2026 converts were repaid in March 2026). Net debt $422.2M. Caveat: the share count (2026-07-27) postdates the cash (2026-06-30), so any July buybacks lower the count without lowering the cash we credit - a small overstatement (each $100M of July buybacks ~ +$2/share). BUYBACKS: Tyler is a repurchaser - $174.7M FY2025, $755.0M in H1-2026 (funded by the new converts), new $1.5B authorization August 2026 - so the flat count is being funded, not merely assumed. Cash taxes have run far below book (FY2025 $40.8M paid on $390M pretax; H1-2026 $16.5M on $227M) because restored immediate R&D expensing (Section 174) lifted deferred taxes; the cash tax path ramps from 12% to 23% by year 5. Acquired-intangible amortisation (~$89M next year, falling to ~$57M by year 5 per the FY2025 10-K schedule) is why D&A glides from 5.6% toward a ~2% steady state, above capex (1.5%) only while that amortisation runs off.",
